          %title Classical Mechanics via Prequantum Correspondences
          %blockquote
            %p
              This entry is a sub-chapter of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
            %p
              The following is effectively a derivation of, and an introduction to,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
              by studying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
              in what is called (as we will explain) the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
                  over the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantized+Lagrangian+correspondence"} prequantized Lagrangian correspondence
              and the reader looking for just these should skip ahead to the section
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#TheClassicalActionFunctionalPrequantizesHamiltonianCorrespondences"} The classical action functional prequantizes Lagrangian correspondences
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
              etc.
