          %h1#classical_mechanics_via_prequantum_correspondences Classical Mechanics via Prequantum Correspondences
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ModelLayer"} Model Layer
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#PhaseSpaceAndSymplecticManifolds"} Phase spaces and symplectic manifolds
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#CanonicalTransformations"} Canonical transformations and symplectomorphisms
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#TrajectoriesAndLagrangianCorrespondences"} Trajectories and Lagrangian correspondences
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#defininition"} Defininition
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#TheClassicalActionFunctionalPrequantizesHamiltonianCorrespondences"} Hamiltonian (time evolution) trajectories and Hamiltonian correspondences
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#KineticAction"} The kinetic action and Planck’s constant
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#Prequantization"} Pre-Quantization and Differential cohomology
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HamiltonianTrajectoriesAndPrequantizedLagrangianCorrespondences"} Hamiltonian flows, the Legendre transform and the Hamilton-Jacobi action
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#heisenberg_group_and_poisson_bracket"} Heisenberg group and Poisson bracket
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#hamiltonian_actions_and_moment_maps"} Hamiltonian actions and moment maps
              %li
                %a{:href => "#SemanticsLayer"} Semantic Layer
              %li
                %a{:href => "#SyntacticLayer"} Syntactic Layer
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#ModelLayer Model Layer
          %p
            Here we discuss the notion of
            %em prequantized Lagrangian correspondences
            and how it serves to embed traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
            in its formulation as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian mechanics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+mechanics"} Lagrangian mechanics
            into the general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            and its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
          %p
            A traditional notion is that of a plain
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondence"} Lagrangian correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifold"} Lagrangian submanifold
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            and another one, with opposite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondences"} Lagrangian correspondences
            naturally generalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphisms"} symplectomorphisms
            – hence transformations between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            – via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
          %p
            But in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            proper, and in particular with an eye towards
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            of these symplectic manifolds by lifting them to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+bundles"} prequantum circle bundles
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %em prequantized Lagrangian correspondence
            is the refinement of that of plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondence"} Lagrangian correspondence
            which does properly respect and reflect this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            information: a prequantized Lagrangian correspondence is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+subspace"} Lagrangian subspace
            as before, but now equipped with an explicit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            between the pullbacks of the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+bundles"} prequantum circle bundles
            to the correspondence space.
          %p
            We discuss below how the concept of prequantized Lagrangian correspondences neatly induces and unifies ingredients and aspects of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian mechanics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+mechanics"} Lagrangian mechanics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
            associated to it via the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Legendre+transform"} Legendre transform
            %em
              %a{:href => "#TheClassicalActionFunctionalPrequantizesHamiltonianCorrespondences"} The classical action prequantizes Hamiltonian correspondences
            we see that prequantized Lagrangian correspondences are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            which schematically express this data as follows:
