                    \\\
                    X_1 &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X_2
                    }
          %h3#TheClassicalActionFunctionalPrequantizesHamiltonianCorrespondences Hamiltonian (time evolution) trajectories and Hamiltonian correspondences
          %p
            An important class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphisms"} symplectomorphisms
            are the following
          #HamiltonianCorrespondence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-,-\}
              takes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \in C^\infty(X)
              (the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"}> Hamiltonian
              ”) to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{H,-\}
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi H
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_H \in \Gamma T X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphisms"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms
              from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
              to itself, is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphism"} symplectomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flow"} flow
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
              for some parameter “time”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\exp( t \{H,-\}) \;\colon\; (X,\omega) \longrightarrow (X,\omega)
                    \\,.
            %p
              We call a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondence"} Lagrangian correspondence
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianCorrespondence"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphisms"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %em Hamiltonian correspondences
          #HamiltonianCorrespondencesAreSpacesOfTrajectories.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Under the interpretation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
              as spaces of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
              as in example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctionsAsCorrespondences"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence+space"} correspondence space
              of a Hamiltonian correspondence is naturally identified with the space of
              %em
                classical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fields
                      %mi traj
                      %mi class
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi graph
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi H
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fields_{traj}^{class}(t) = graph\left( \exp(t\{H,-\}) \right)
            %p in that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every point in the space corresponds uniquely to a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectory"} trajectory
                  of parameter time length
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
                  characterized as satisfying the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
                  as given by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamilton%27s+equations"} Hamilton's equations
                  for
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %li
                %p
                  the two projection maps to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  send a trajectory to its initial and to its final configuration, respectively.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Forming Hamiltonian correspondences consitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from 1-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"} Riemannian structure
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+correspondences"} category of correspondences
              in the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
